  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying 'probable' outcomes (with probability strictly greater than 1/n) and comparing the average of such outcomes. However, in this case, no outcome meets the 'probable' criterion under strict interpretation, so the reason cannot produce a preference. Even under a lenient interpretation, the individual does not mention any calculation or consideration of averages of high-probability outcomes. Instead, they focus on the presence of a zero-loss outcome in A and aversion to the certainty of loss in B. Their reasoning aligns more with loss aversion and certainty effect (from prospect theory) than with the specified decision rule. There is no indication that they categorized outcomes by probability thresholds or computed averages of such subsets. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not match the structure or logic of the decision reason.",
